Done. `node --test test/*.test.js` passes all 16 tests.

**Implementation** (only files under `src/`):

- **`src/lexer.js`** — the scanner, exporting `scan(source)`, `ScanError` and `KINDS`. It walks the input as an array of code points, tracking line/column with the tab rule (`col → floor((col-1)/4)*4 + 5`) and line-feed reset. It covers:
  - whitespace, `//` line comments, and nesting `/* … */` block comments (unterminated reported at the outermost opener);
  - identifiers vs. the eight keywords;
  - numbers with `0x/0X`, `0b/0B`, `0o/0O` prefixes or decimal with optional fraction and exponent, `_` only between two digits of one run, and `invalid number <text>` errors that swallow the trailing ident characters (covers `12abc`, `0x`, `1__2`, `1e`);
  - `.` and `e/E` only continuing a number when a digit (or sign then digit) follows;
  - strings with `\n \t \r \\ \" \0 \xHH \u{H…}` (≤ 10FFFF), `invalid escape \c` at the backslash, `newline in string` at the line feed, `unterminated string` at the opening quote;
  - `r"…"` raw strings, unterminated reported at the `r`;
  - punctuation matched longest-first, everything else `unexpected character`.
- **`src/cli.js`** — argument check (`error: usage: cli.js tokens|stats`), reads stdin as UTF-8, and renders either `<line>:<column> <kind> <body>` lines (string/rawstring bodies via `JSON.stringify` of the decoded value) or the six fixed kind counts plus `total N`. Output is built fully before writing, so a failure prints one `error: <line>:<column>: <reason>` line to stderr, nothing to stdout, and exits 2.

No dependencies were added and `node_modules` does not exist.

